{"availability":"available","full":"panique/huge","name":"huge","description":"Simple user-authentication solution, embedded into a small framework.","category":"Developer tools","language":"PHP","stars":2155,"forks":764,"created":"2012-05-06T01:04:43Z","updated":"2024-09-04T22:51:37Z","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["auth","authentication","authorization","framework","password","password-hash","php","user-auth"],"demo":"http://104.131.8.128/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:13.152Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:13.152Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:13.152Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:32:13.152Z","stars":2155,"forks":764}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Just a simple user authentication solution inside a super-simple framework skeleton that works out-of-the-box (and comes with an auto-installer), using the future-proof official bcrypt password hashing/salting implementation of PHP 5.5+, plus some nice features that will speed up the time from idea to first usable prototype application dramatically. Nothing more. This project has its focus on hardcore simplicity. Everything is as simple as possible, made for smaller projects, typical agency work and quick drafts. If you want to build massive corporate applications with all the features modern…","HUGE's simple-as-possible architecture was inspired by several conference talks, slides and articles about huge applications that - surprisingly and intentionally - go back to the basics of programming, using procedural programming, static classes, extremely simple constructs, not-totally-DRY code etc. while keeping the code extremely readable (StackOverflow, Wikipedia, SoundCloud).","Some interesting Buzzwords in this context: KISS, YAGNI, Feature Creep, Minimum viable product."],"features":["built with the official PHP password hashing functions, fitting the most modern password hashing/salting web standards","proper sec